  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Women&#x2019;s Rights, Qualitative participation &amp; freedom from violence-KtK</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till &quot;F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter i Rwanda, 2017-2019 (KtK)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna har ans&#xf6;kt om 39 464 068 kr fr&#xe5;n Sida f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;rande av projektet &quot;Enhancing Women&apos;s Rights Protection, Qualitative Participation and Freedom from Violence in Rwanda, 2017-2019&quot;. Projektet syftar till att bidra till ett samh&#xe4;lle d&#xe4;r alla former av k&#xf6;nsdiskriminering  har upph&#xf6;rt, d&#xe4;r kvinnor deltar obehindrat i beslutsfattande och konfliktl&#xf6;sning och d&#xe4;r kvinnors m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter respekteras. Projektets tre huvudsakliga resultat p&#xe5; outcome-niv&#xe5; &#xe4;r: 1) St&#xe4;rkt skydd mot k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld med speciellt fokus p&#xe5; f&#xf6;rebyggande;2) F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad kvalitet i kvinnors politiska och ekonomiska deltagande och deltagande i konfliktl&#xf6;sning; 3) St&#xe4;rkt kapacitet hos Kvinna till Kvinnas partnerorganisationer att arbeta effektivt och b&#xe4;rkraftigt.

Den totala projektbudgeten, avrundad upp&#xe5;t till 40 miljoner kronor, kommer att t&#xe4;ckas av Sida. Skillnaden p&#xe5; cirka 500 000 kronor mellan KtK:s f&#xf6;reslagna budget och den totala projektbudgeten f&#xf6;rklaras av ett behov av medel f&#xf6;r att t&#xe4;cka kostnader f&#xf6;r en halvtids&#xf6;versyn och en s&#xe4;rskild revisorsgranskning av avtalen mellan KtK och dess partnerorganisationer. Totalt 15 miljoner kronor kommer att avst&#xe4;ttas av Kvinna till Kvinna f&#xf6;r vidaref&#xf6;rmedling till 6-8 partnerorganisationer, som kommer att identifieras under projektets inledningsfas f&#xf6;rsta halv&#xe5;ret 2017.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvinna till Kvinna has submitted to the embassy of Sweden in Kigali  a project proposal worth a total budget of 39 464 068 SEK to implement  a project entitled &quot; Enhancing Women&#x2019;s Rights, Qualitative Participation and Freedom from Violence in Rwanda, 2017-2019&quot;. 

The project aims at contributing to having &#x201c;A society where all forms of discrimination based on gender has been eradicated, where women participate fully in decision-making and conflict resolution, and where women&#x2019;s rights are respected.&#x201d; This will be achieved in Rwanda through implementation of three main outcomes: 1) Improved protection from gender-based violence with a specific focus on prevention; 2) Enhanced women&#x2019;s qualitative participation in political and economic decision-making and conflict resolution; and 3) Increased capacity of Kvinna till Kvinna&#x2019;s partner organisations to operate effectively and sustainably.

The total project budget of maximum 40 million SEK will be funded by Sida. The deviation of approximately 500 000 SEK compared to KtK&apos;s proposed budget is explained by the need for extra funds to cover costs for a Mid Term Review and for a pre-audit of the Agreements between KtK and its partner organisations. A total of 15 million SEK will be forwarded to the yet to be selected 6 to 8 local partner organisations in 3 years and the amount of funds to be forwarded to each organisation will be determined after selection and individual planning and budgeting.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The change expected to be achieved in 2019 following the implementation of the five year project for &quot;Enhancing Womens Rights Protection, Qualitative Participation and Freedom from Violence in Rwanda&quot; implemented by Kvinna till kvinna, is A society where all forms of discrimination based on gender has been eradicated, where women participate fully in decision-making and conflict resolution, and where women&apos;s rights are respected. 

Specific outcomes are listed below. 
 
(Outcome 1)Improved protection from gender-based violence with a specific focus on prevention.
(Outcome 2) Enhanced women&apos;s qualitative participation in decision-making and conflict resolution.
(Outcome 3) Increased capacity of Kvinna till Kvinna&apos;s partner organisations to operate effectively and sustainably 

Improved protection from Gender based Violence (GBV) with a specific focus on prevention when Men, boys, women and girls targeted by sensitization activities are expected to acknowledge positive changes in attitudes and/or behavior regarding GBV.

The enhancement of women&apos;s qualitative participation in decision-making and conflict resolution  when targeted women participate qualitatively in decision-making and/or in conflict resolution at different levels.

Capacity strengthening of Kvinna till Kvinnas  selected partner organisations enabling them  to operate effectively and sustainably through strengthening  in accordance with the Organisational Capacity Assessment Tool. This will also be assessed by Kvinna till Kvinnas perception regarding positive changes in partner organisations&apos; capacity to operate effectively and sustainably.</narrative>
  </description>
